class Solution {
    public int countSubstrings(String s) {
        int result = 0;
        if (s.length() == 0)
            return 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {
            int left = i;
            int right = i;

            result = result + isPal(s, i, i);//odd number palindrome check

            result = result + isPal(s, left, right + 1);// even number palindrome check

        }
        return result;
    }

    int isPal(String s, int left, int right) {
        int result = 0;
        while (left >= 0 && right < s.length() && s.charAt(left) == s.charAt(right)) {
            result++;
            left--;
            right++;
        }
        return result;
    }
}

//CODE END
A string of length $N$ has 2N - 1 potential centers for palindromes (N single-character centers for odd-length
palindromes and N - 1 center pairs for even-length palindromes).


For each center, the helper method isPal expands outward using two pointers (l and r).
In the worst-case scenario (e.g., when the string consists of identical characters like "aaaaa"),
expanding from a center can take O(N) operations.

Total Operations: Summing the expansion steps across all 2N - 1 centers yields O(N times N) = O(N^2) time complexity, where N is the length of 
the string s


Space Complexity: O(1)The solution expands directly on the input string using two integer pointers (l and r) without
allocating any extra dynamic data structures or recursion call stacks.

